Rule 1 (input must be a tensor to avoid TypeError)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 2 (in-place acos requires floating or complex dtype to avoid cast error)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10
>>
Rule 3 (real inputs kept within acos domain to avoid NaNs)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 then min(v_1) ≥ -1 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 1
>>
Rule 4 (all dimensions of the input tensor are positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
